From: Shimazu <vanessimbolon2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 02:19:04 +0000
Subject: GListeners: Replace legacy ItemStack data-value constructor with named materials

AE PATCH REASON: Legacy ItemStack(Material, int, short) damage-value constructor is deprecated and removed on modern Bukkit/Paper versions after the 1.13 flattening; it fails to compile against current Paper API.
AE PATCH FIX: Replace new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)5) with LIME_STAINED_GLASS in the remove-item GUI and drop the meaningless (short)5 data value from the REDSTONE_BLOCK confirm-delete item.
AE PATCH RISK: LOW - API: legacy ItemStack damage-value constructor → named materials. No behavior change.

---
diff --git a/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GListeners.java b/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GListeners.java
--- a/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GListeners.java	2026-07-30 10:27:31.681350240 +0000
+++ b/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GListeners.java	2026-07-31 00:31:13.779403980 +0000
@@ -41,11 +41,11 @@
                   }
 
                   Inventory var6 = Bukkit.createInventory(new GListeners.GInvHolder(), 27, "§eRemove from " + var4);
-                  ItemStack var7 = new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)5);
+                  ItemStack var7 = new ItemStack(Material.LIME_STAINED_GLASS);
                   ItemMeta var8 = var7.getItemMeta();
                   var8.setDisplayName("§aRemove Item from GKit");
                   var7.setItemMeta(var8);
-                  ItemStack var9 = new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)5);
+                  ItemStack var9 = new ItemStack(Material.LIME_STAINED_GLASS);
                   ItemMeta var10 = var9.getItemMeta();
                   var10.setDisplayName("§aRemove Item from GKit");
                   var9.setItemMeta(var10);
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
                   if (var1.getCurrentItem().getType().equals(Material.ENDER_CHEST)) {
                      new GEditorContent(var3, var15).openInventory();
                   } else if (var1.getCurrentItem().getType().equals(Material.REDSTONE_BLOCK)) {
-                     ItemStack var17 = new ItemStack(Material.REDSTONE_BLOCK, 1, (short)5);
+                     ItemStack var17 = new ItemStack(Material.REDSTONE_BLOCK);
                      ItemMeta var18 = var17.getItemMeta();
                      var18.setDisplayName("§aConfirm to delete GKit");
                      var17.setItemMeta(var18);
